🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
NCCL custom kernels accepts a ncclWindow_t argument as representation of a symmetric memory range.
To support op developers, the following code support (in C++) is needed:
// C++ function of an all_reduce op
void all_reduce_func(Tensor x, const std::string& group) {
  auto handle = symmetric_memory::rendezvous(x, group);
  // A tensor's starting address is fixed by a window and an offset to the window base
  auto window = handle.get_window();
  size_t offset = handle.get_offset();
  allReduceKernel<<<...>>>(window, offset);
}

Today SymmMem handle supports get_offset, but does not offer get_window yet.
Note that since window is specific to NCCL instead of NVSHMEM or CUDA backend, we can leave it a backend specific method. Op developer would then cast handle into a derived NCCLSymmetricMemory pointer first before accessing this method.
